{"seq":1,"slug":"testing-in-the-agent-era","title":"Testing In The Agent Era","docCount":3,"url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-testing/testing-in-the-agent-era","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-tests-matter-more-with-agents","title":"为什么有了 Agent 测试更重要","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-testing/testing-in-the-agent-era/why-tests-matter-more-with-agents","wordCount":2106,"readingTime":9},{"seq":2,"slug":"tests-as-executable-spec","title":"测试作为可执行的规格","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-testing/testing-in-the-agent-era/tests-as-executable-spec","wordCount":1967,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"tests-as-agent-guardrail","title":"测试作为 Agent 的护栏","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-testing/testing-in-the-agent-era/tests-as-agent-guardrail","wordCount":1944,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章讲清测试在 agent 时代为什么不降反升地重要:agent 大量快速产出代码、人审不过来,测试成了替人确认「改动对不对」的中坚;一份测试同时扮演三个角色——它是把「这段代码该做什么」固定下来的可执行规格(agent 读测试就知道意图)、是 agent 写完能立刻据它自我纠错的反馈源、也是合入前挡住坏代码的护栏。理解这三重角色,才明白为什么「先把测试做好」是让 agent 放心改代码的前提。\n"}